@startuml Historical Trends Sequence Diagram
title Figure X: Historical Optimization Trends Sequence Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #fff9e6
    BorderColor #d4a017
    FontSize 11
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "Dashboard / Cost UI" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "SupabaseDashboardService" as Service <<Control>>
database "Supabase DB" as DB <<Database>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Select "Trends" or Load Analytics Page
activate UI

UI -> Service : getOptimizationHistory(limit)
activate Service

Service -> DB : SELECT * FROM dashboard_optimization_history\nORDER BY timestamp DESC
activate DB
DB --> Service : List of raw history records
deactivate DB

Service -> Service : mapHistoryFromDb(records)
note right : Normalizes database snake_case\nto frontend camelCase.

Service --> UI : Array of normalized HistoryEntries
deactivate Service

UI -> UI : Aggregate Data for Charts
note right : Groups savings by Month/Week\nCalculates moving averages\nfor efficiency (kW/ton).

UI -> UI : Render BarChart / LineChart (Recharts)

UI --> User : Display Historical Performance Trends
deactivate UI

note right of Service
  **Performance Optimization:**
  Queries are limited and ordered
  to ensure the dashboard remains
  responsive even with thousands
  of historical records.
end note

@enduml
